From: Manoj Kumar Prabakaran <manojkumar.prabakaran@arm.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 16:48:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 24/28] platform-mc: add helper to get terminus name

Add a Manager helper to look up a discovered terminus by TID and
return the terminus name from its Entity Auxiliary Names PDR.

The helper lets OEM handlers map an incoming event's TID to the stable
platform identity advertised by the terminus. TID and MCTP EID are
assigned during discovery and can change across rediscovery or transport
topology changes, while the MCTP network ID identifies the transport
instance and a sensor name identifies the sensor rather than the
terminus.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/pldm/+/91864]

Change-Id: Ib6a3ce08f6354cf14bcd2e11fc9e6ebc02097509
Signed-off-by: Manoj Kumar Prabakaran <manojkumar.prabakaran@arm.com>
---
 platform-mc/manager.hpp | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/platform-mc/manager.hpp b/platform-mc/manager.hpp
index 056d7bc..6474180 100644
--- a/platform-mc/manager.hpp
+++ b/platform-mc/manager.hpp
@@ -10,6 +10,10 @@
 
 #include <libpldm/pldm.h>
 
+#include <optional>
+#include <string>
+#include <string_view>
+
 namespace pldm
 {
 namespace platform_mc
@@ -237,6 +241,22 @@ class Manager : public pldm::MctpDiscoveryHandlerIntf
         eventManager.registerPolledEventHandler(eventClass, handlers);
     }
 
+    /** @brief Get terminus name by terminus ID
+     *
+     *  @param[in] tid - Terminus ID
+     *  @return terminus name when a matching terminus exists
+     */
+    std::optional<std::string_view> getTerminusName(pldm_tid_t tid)
+    {
+        auto terminus = termini.find(tid);
+        if (terminus == termini.end() || !terminus->second)
+        {
+            return std::nullopt;
+        }
+
+        return terminus->second->getTerminusName();
+    }
+
     /** @brief Register OEM flow to poll the PLDM Event use
      *         PollForPlatformEventMessage command
      *
